    "narrative": "Our lineup for May 29th is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who carries an elite 74.98 score into his matchup against Samaniego. He remains our most reliable asset given his prime batting order position and high floor. Joining him at the top of our output projections are **Matt Chapman** (69.75) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable park environment against Lorenzen. While we are currently awaiting official lineups for those spots, the expectation is that their presence in the top half of the order will maximize their high xwOBA profiles today. **Jonathan Aranda** also provides a strong 66.12, taking advantage of a high-ceiling matchup against Ure\u00f1a, where his dynamic platoon splits and projected #2 hole production provide the leverage we need to stay competitive in R&B/RBI counts.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the bench today involved **Geraldo Perdomo**, who finished just outside the starting cut with a 45.64 score. While his potential for stolen bases is an attractive asset given our scarcity focus, the combination of a difficult matchup against the sharp pitching of Kirby and a cooling trend in his recent production pushed him behind the likes of **Masyn Winn** and **Tyler Freeman**. We are closely monitoring the status of **Will Smith**; his projection is suppressed (45.76) due to an arduous matchup against the elite Zack Wheeler, though we are leaning on the 5% wind-out factor to potentially buoy his power numbers. Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding **Lawrence Butler** and **Daulton Varsho**, as both face high-skill lefties that dampen their base projections, though their park factors keep them in the mix for the daily cap. \n\nWe continue to monitor the long-term outlook for our IL-bound core of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**, as their absence remains a significant drain on our positional flexibility. With **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Gleyber Torres** currently outside the starting rotation, we are maintaining a disciplined approach to our game caps. If the pending lineups for **Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Lawrence Butler** shift downward in the batting order, expect us to pivot quickly to maximize efficiency, as any drop in order seniority significantly impacts our overall scoring density.",
